---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/product.css';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="PLM and revisions" description="Projects, revisions with notes, supporting artifacts, and a project graph that shows how your documents are connected.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product / Collaborate</p>
      <h1>One design, one identity, and the history that explains it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A project is the boundary for designs, assemblies, manufacturing artifacts, and revision history. Chudware keeps the sequence of decisions attached to the geometry, so a handoff carries the deliverable and the reasoning behind it.</p>
      <ul class="product-hero-meta">
        <li>Revisions with notes, not <code>_final_v7</code> filenames</li>
        <li>Specifications, photos, reports, and supplier files as project items</li>
        <li>Project graph, history timeline, and revision compare</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="history-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow" id="history-title">Revision history</p>
        <h2>History is a line you can walk back.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Save a checkpoint when a design decision is ready to preserve, and use the note to explain why the design changed and what evidence you checked. The design keeps one identity; history carries the sequence.</p>
      </header>
      <figure class="product-diagram">
        <svg class="product-svg" viewBox="0 0 640 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="plm-diagram-title">
          <title id="plm-diagram-title">A project timeline: four checkpoints on one design identity, each carrying a note, with supporting artifacts attached to the checkpoints they belong to.</title>
          <defs>
            <marker id="plm-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="product-svg-arrow-accent" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z" />
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <text class="product-svg-label-faint" x="40" y="30">PROJECT &middot; ONE DESIGN IDENTITY</text>

          <line class="product-svg-hidden" x1="60" y1="120" x2="590" y2="120" />

          <line class="product-svg-flow" x1="130" y1="120" x2="240" y2="120" marker-end="url(#plm-arrow)" />
          <line class="product-svg-flow" x1="280" y1="120" x2="390" y2="120" marker-end="url(#plm-arrow)" />
          <line class="product-svg-flow" x1="430" y1="120" x2="530" y2="120" marker-end="url(#plm-arrow)" />

          <circle class="product-svg-node" cx="110" cy="120" r="17" />
          <circle class="product-svg-node" cx="260" cy="120" r="17" />
          <circle class="product-svg-node" cx="410" cy="120" r="17" />
          <circle class="product-svg-node-accent" cx="550" cy="120" r="17" />
          <text class="product-svg-title" x="110" y="125" text-anchor="middle">A</text>
          <text class="product-svg-title" x="260" y="125" text-anchor="middle">B</text>
          <text class="product-svg-title" x="410" y="125" text-anchor="middle">C</text>
          <text class="product-svg-title" x="550" y="125" text-anchor="middle">D</text>

          <text class="product-svg-label" x="110" y="84" text-anchor="middle">first layout</text>
          <text class="product-svg-label" x="260" y="84" text-anchor="middle">wall thickened</text>
          <text class="product-svg-label" x="410" y="84" text-anchor="middle">bolt circle set</text>
          <text class="product-svg-label-dim" x="550" y="84" text-anchor="middle">current</text>

          <line class="product-svg-con" x1="110" y1="137" x2="110" y2="190" />
          <line class="product-svg-con" x1="260" y1="137" x2="260" y2="190" />
          <line class="product-svg-con" x1="410" y1="137" x2="410" y2="190" />
          <line class="product-svg-con" x1="550" y1="137" x2="550" y2="190" />

          <rect class="product-svg-node" x="58" y="190" width="104" height="40" rx="3" />
          <rect class="product-svg-node" x="208" y="190" width="104" height="40" rx="3" />
          <rect class="product-svg-node" x="358" y="190" width="104" height="40" rx="3" />
          <rect class="product-svg-node" x="498" y="190" width="104" height="40" rx="3" />
          <text class="product-svg-label" x="110" y="215" text-anchor="middle">SPEC</text>
          <text class="product-svg-label" x="260" y="215" text-anchor="middle">DRAWING</text>
          <text class="product-svg-label" x="410" y="215" text-anchor="middle">CAM OUTPUT</text>
          <text class="product-svg-label" x="550" y="215" text-anchor="middle">SUPPLIER PDF</text>

          <text class="product-svg-label-faint" x="40" y="268">EACH CHECKPOINT CARRIES A NOTE: WHAT CHANGED, AND WHAT WAS CHECKED</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>Checkpoints on one identity, with supporting artifacts attached where they were produced.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="project-title">
    <div class="wrap product-columns">
      <div>
        <header class="section-heading product-subhead">
          <p class="eyebrow" id="project-title">Inside a project</p>
          <h2>Keep related work under one root.</h2>
        </header>
        <p class="product-body">Native <code>.step+</code> files belong under the project root so Chudware can connect them without relying on absolute paths. Design files register through their save and checkpoint flow; supporting non-design files are added as project items.</p>
        <p class="product-body">That distinction matters at handoff. A supplier PDF and a photo of a failed print are evidence, and they should sit beside the revision they justify rather than in someone's mailbox.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-spec-wrap">
        <table class="product-spec">
          <caption>What a project holds</caption>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Designs</th><td>Native <code>.step+</code> parts and assemblies under the project root</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">History</th><td>Checkpoints with revision notes, newest first</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Artifacts</th><td>Specifications, photos, reports, supplier files as project items</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Manufacturing</th><td>Job output produced from the designs in the same project</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Compare</th><td>An item at two history points, including a rendered geometry diff</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="graph-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow" id="graph-title">Project graph</p>
        <h2>See how the documents are actually connected.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The PLM workspace renders the project as a node-and-edge graph: documents and related items as nodes, their relationships as edges. You can search it, scope into a single node and its neighbors, or switch to a grid view with rendered document previews.</p>
        <p class="supporting-copy">Jumping from a part in the Feature Manager to that part's links in the graph is one click.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="product-note">
        <p class="eyebrow">Before a handoff</p>
        <ul class="fact-list">
          <li>Checkpoint the design so the recipient starts from a known state</li>
          <li>Confirm every referenced part is available in the project</li>
          <li>Include the relevant drawing, neutral export, or manufacturing output</li>
          <li>Leave the decision trail intact &mdash; the notes are the handoff</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/plm/">PLM guide <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Next</p>
      <h2>Give the work a project before it needs one.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Install the desktop app, or read how the copilot operates inside the same documents and history.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/download/">Download</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/product/copilot/">The AI copilot</a></div>
      <ul class="product-jump">
        <li><a href="/product/">All capabilities</a></li>
        <li><a href="/product/modeling/">Modeling</a></li>
        <li><a href="/product/assemblies/">Assemblies</a></li>
        <li><a href="/product/cam/">CAM</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/plm/">Docs</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
